g_path\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"component\",\n      \"name\": \"observer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"component\",\n      \"name\": \"memorypipeline\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"component\",\n      \"name\": \"cognee memory layer\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n[2026-07-04T16:47:39.956561]\nQUESTION: Provide a high-level summary of the architecture\nANSWER: {\n  \"answer\": \"The system is a local-first background memory service that continuously builds and maintains a project's knowledge graph. Its high-level data flow is: Developer actions \u2192 Observer Service (passively detects events, never interprets) \u2192 Event Intelligence (filters out noise such as build folders, caches) \u2192 Memory Pipeline (normalizes events, deduplicates, optionally extracts reasoning via an LLM Provider, then stores structured knowledge via cognee.remember()) \u2192 Cognee Memory Layer (the source of truth, storing knowledge graph, vector embeddings, and metadata in embedded SQLite, LanceDB, and KuzuDB) \u2192 Memory Orchestrator (constructs retrieval requests, calls cognee.recall(), returns normalized output) \u2192 Dashboard (human-facing visualizations) and MCP Server (AI\u2011assistant interface). Key architectural rules enforce a strict separation of concerns: the Observer never interprets, Event Intelligence never stores, the Memory Pipeline never answers questions, Cognee owns all memory, the Orchestrator only orchestrates retrieval, the Dashboard only visualizes, and the MCP Server only exposes memory to external AI tools. Additional guidelines include a unified dataset per project, manual decision notes that bypass the Observer, scheduled improvement cycles, and deterministic graph visualizations that avoid heavyweight exports.\",\n  \"reasoning_path\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"document\",\n      \"name\": \"This chunk is about: - Projects: engraph (Cognee) system - Products: Cognee - Companies: Nvidia - Roles: Developer, Architecture Owner - Concepts: Local-first, Source of Truth, Reasoning Extraction - Components: Observer Service, Event Intelligence, Memory Pipeline, LLM Provider, Cognee Memory, Memory Orchestrator, Dashboard, MCP Server - Events: Git commits, file modifications\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"document\",\n      \"name\": \"ARCHITECTURE.md\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n[2026-07-04T17:02:13.200960]\nQUESTION: What are the recent architectural decisions?\nANSWER: [{\"decision\":\"Built a standalone FastAPI sidecar (Decoupled NIM Gateway) to intercept, sanitize, and translate OpenAI-formatted payloads into strict NVIDIA NIM schemas in real-time.\",\"reason\":\"Prevents event-loop deadlocks and ensures lightning-fast graph ingestion without relying on fragile CLI proxies.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: README.md Status:... [graph, ai, project]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Built the foundational MCP (Model Context Protocol) server for universal AI compatibility.\",\"reason\":\"To allow any compatible AI tool to instantly read the project\u2019s mind.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: README.md Status:... [graph, ai, project]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Created Multi-Hop Detective UI component that traverses the knowledge graph to answer complex architectural questions with live reasoning trace paths.\",\"reason\":\"To provide zero-load reasoning trace visualization, answering complex graph questions without added backend load or latency.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: README.md Status:... [graph, ai, project]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Implemented deterministic graph visualization API (/api/graph/summary) that returns a pruned, fast subgraph in <0.1s.\",\"reason\":\"To avoid crashing the browser with massive unstructured graph pull and achieve rapid rendering.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: README.md Status:... [graph, ai, project]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Implemented self-healing indexing via a robust startup verification protocol against Cognee.\",\"reason\":\"To ensure the Knowledge Graph is perfectly synced and prevent rate-limit flooding on reboot.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: README.md Status:... [graph, ai, project]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Implemented ticking debt detection to monitor 'ghost decisions' (code written without recorded intent).\",\"reason\":\"To nudge developers before knowledge is lost.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: README.md Status:... [graph, ai, project]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Designed the system to be local-first, using LanceDB + KuzuDB for embeddings and graph traversal, backed by Nvidia AI API for reasoning extraction.\",\"reason\":\"To run embeddings and graph traversal entirely local, ensuring fast and private operation.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: README.md Status:... [graph, ai, project]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Enforced the Unified Dataset Rule: every project uses exactly ONE unified dataset to ensure a connected knowledge graph.\",\"reason\":\"To prevent the Knowledge Graph from fracturing across multiple Cognee namespaces.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Established a two-tier capture system: Tier 1 automatic observation, Tier 2 manual decision notes only.\",\"reason\":\"To separate automatic observation from manual decision capture.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Designed the Observer to be passive; it never interprets events.\",\"reason\":\"To keep observation pure and avoid inference.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"}]\n\n[2026-07-04T17:11:17.172738]\nQUESTION: What are the recent architectural decisions?\nANSWER: [\n  {\n    \"decision\": \"Manual notes are normalized directly as MANUAL_NOTE events, bypassing the file observer.\",\n    \"reason\": \"to ensure accurate decision capture\",\n    \"source\": \"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\n    \"confidence\": \"Confirmed\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"decision\": \"Nudge suppression checks globally across all paths for recent manual decisions.\",\n    \"reason\": \"offering a better developer experience (i.e. \\\"I already explained my reasoning today\\\")\",\n    \"source\": \"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\n    \"confidence\": \"Confirmed\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"decision\": \"Memory Pipeline stages: Normalizer \u2192 Deduplicator \u2192 two paths (reasoning to extract \u2192 LLM Interpretation \u2192 cognee.remember() node_set=decisions; structural change only \u2192 cognee.remember() directly).\",\n    \"reason\": \"to separate reasoning extraction from structural changes and prevent redundant remember() calls\",\n    \"source\": \"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\n    \"confidence\": \"Confirmed\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"decision\": \"Deduplicator prevents redundant remember() calls using content hashing + SQLite log.\",\n    \"reason\": \"to prevent stale state accumulation in the graph\",\n    \"source\": \"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\n    \"confidence\": \"Confirmed\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"decision\": \"Initial indexing runs on first project registration: backfills last 50 commits and existing docs/deps.\",\n    \"reason\": \"to quickly build the knowledge graph from existing project history\",